      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith radix caching disabled, ordinary token requests and `input_embeds` requests are individually supported. Concurrent requests can share a normal causal prefill batch. The batch gathers all token IDs but only supplied embedding rows, then gives that shorter embedding tensor to the whole forward.\n\nA two-token ordinary request plus three supplied embedding rows creates five KV locations for only three input vectors. A native CPU KV write fails on that mismatch; a single supplied row can instead broadcast incorrect values into another request's slots.\n\n## Modifications\n\nExtend the existing scheduler pooling-mode compatibility guard to preserve one input form per forward. Incompatible requests remain queued before their preemption/cache/initialization path, while later compatible requests can still batch together. This also preserves a resumed chunk's input form.\n\nNearby diffs #20376 (chunk slicing/prefill-decode mixing), #45041 (decode cleanup), #47493 (DP padding), #40745 (sessions) and #43681 (width validation) cover separate cases.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nTested base: `fd19cfb660f42bd3ceb6df7598bd343572e30d2c`. At publication, main has advanced by one documentation-only commit; the runtime, policy and test files are unchanged.\n\n- Four new native scheduler subcases fail on the base. The candidate passes 68 tests and 66 subtests across the scheduler admission/running-request and PrefillAdder suites.\n- A separate 120-case CPU queue/KV replay has 88 base failures and zero candidate failures. It uses actual Scheduler selection, PrefillAdder, batch construction, ModelRunner embedding kwargs and MHATokenToKVPool writes/readback. It verifies per-request vectors and recovery of request/token slots, including both input orders, interleaved queues, one-row broadcasting and ignore_eos.\n- Independent review passes 34/34 selected cases (base fails 24), including 24 physical KV scenarios and eight chunk-continuation cases. Scheduler canaries cover both pooling/input-form compatibility axes and early preemption/prefetch/init exclusion.\n- Torch 2.14.1+cpu. Source/import/native-library bindings were checked before and after the component proofs. A local embedding table and identity K/V projection isolate the row/value contract; full-model and GPU execution were not run.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nMixed input forms require separate prefill batches. Later compatible requests still join the current batch. No throughput improvement is claimed.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Changed-file pre-commit hooks pass.\n- [x] Compact regression extends the existing scheduler admission fixture.\n- [x] Normal causal-prefill component scope and execution limits are stated.\n\nI directed this work and take responsibility for the contribution and its follow-up. AI assistance was used in producing the change.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41865520921](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41865520921)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41865520439](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41865520439)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41865520688](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41865520688)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
